+**The two screen-space windows.** The deposit is multiplied by `w_in · w_out`, both functions
+of `r` (quarter-res pixels from the sprite centre) alone. Neither is decoration: each removes an
+artefact that is a property of the RASTERIZATION, not of the physics.
+
+* `w_out = 1 − smoothstep(0.8, 1.0, r / R_sprite)`. The sprite is a square quad and the `1/u²`
+  extrapolation is still finite at its boundary, so without a window the quad's edge is a hard
+  cut and every small emitter wears a **white square frame**. Feathering the last 20 % of the
+  radius and zeroing everything beyond it (the quad's corners, `r` up to `√2 R`) makes the
+  cut-off round and invisible. Energy: it takes rather more than half of the last fifth of the
+  logarithmic tail, so the CPU's diagnostic tail estimate integrates to `0.9 R` —
+  `T_tail = c_tail · ln(0.9 R_sprite / R_tex)`.
+* `w_in = smoothstep(0, 2, r)`, i.e. a fade-in over the first 2 quarter-res pixels (8 native).
+  The deposit target is quarter resolution and, just outside the removed core, the pattern falls
+  as `1/u²` from about six kernel texels ≈ 1.4 native pixels — a slope that crosses a whole
+  quarter-res texel in almost nothing, which shows as **4×4 native blocks** around the source.
+  (The analytic streaks never exposed this: their exponential falloff is orders of magnitude
+  gentler.) That radius already belongs to the source itself and to the bloom around it, so
+  fading the glare in over it costs nothing visible. It is **not** free in energy: it is the
+  steepest part of the pattern. The kernel's own core removal (2.5 Airy radii) is unchanged, so
+  the accounting of §2.4 stands and this is a small extra deficit at the very centre — not
+  estimated, because it needs the kernel's radial profile, which lives on the job side; the pass
+  logs the window's radius in kernel texels instead.
+
+If quarter-res blocks survive the inner window, the next step — deliberately not taken — is to
+run the sprite pass into a half-resolution target of its own and composite that down. That is a
+memory and bandwidth decision, not a windowing one.
+
 `kernelLod(u, θ, lod)` samples `$DiffractionKernel` with `SampleLevel` at
 `0.5 + u/L · (cos θ, sin θ)`; `ring(θ)` samples `$DiffractionRing` at `θ / 2π` (bilinear, wrap).
 The kernel's sampler must be **`TrilinearClamp`** — CRYENGINE builds `FILTER_LINEAR` samplers
 with `MaxLOD = 0`, which would silently pin every `SampleLevel` back to level 0 and undo the
 whole chain. Constants: `DiffractionParams0 = (R_sprite_px, s_q, R_tex, norm)`,
-`DiffractionParams1 = (dispersion, L, maxLod = mips − 1, 0)`, and the six
+`DiffractionParams1 = (dispersion, L, maxLod = mips − 1, r_HDRDiffractionDebug)`, and the six
 `colour_λ · (λ₀/λ)²` as a `float4[6]` array (rgb + `λ₀/λ`). The debug view
 (`r_HDRDiffractionDebug`) deliberately stays on level 0: it is there to show the kernel's true
 structure, not what a pixel averages out of it.
 
+`r_HDRDiffractionDebug 2` (shape only) replaces the deposit with a **decade map** of the
+spectral sum, `v = saturate((log10 I + 13) / 10)`. It cannot reuse the corner view's
+`log(1 + I·10⁶)`: that gain is calibrated for the kernel read at level 0, where a ray texel is
+around `1e-4`, whereas what reaches the sprite is the pixel's footprint MEAN (17 texels at f/16,
+100 wide open) plus the `1/u²` tail — `1e-4` down to `1e-12`, which the old curve mapped to
+0.0007, i.e. black. Mode 2 still applies both windows: they are geometry, and the mode exists to
+show the figure the pass actually rasterizes. `r_HDRDiffractionDebug 3` (the thresholded sources
+in the corner) takes a **5×5 max over the source's own texel grid**: the panel is a half-size
+copy of a quarter-resolution texture, so it minifies 2:1 and a one- or two-texel source is point-
+sampled away three times out of four — the panel came up black with a lamp blazing in the frame.
+The max also dilates, so one hot texel paints a 3×3 block of panel pixels, and the panel carries
+a dim floor and a border so that "nothing cleared the threshold" and "the pass never ran" are not
+the same black rectangle.
+
